import datetime,json
from nano_audio.utils import ROOT,write_json,sha
out=ROOT/'artifacts/grpo_attempt_20261107'
def load(path):return json.loads(path.read_text()) if path.exists() else None
attempts={name:{'result':load(folder/'result.json'),'comparison':load(folder/'comparison.json'),'intervals':load(folder/'comparison_intervals.json'),'weight_changes':load(folder/'weight_changes.json')} for name,folder in [('first',out),('strong_init',out/'strong_init')]}
now=datetime.datetime.now(datetime.timezone.utc)
deadline=datetime.datetime(2026,11,7,9,22,35,tzinfo=datetime.timezone.utc)
summary={'study':'exact-reward GRPO continuation','budget_start_utc':'2026-11-07T08:22:35Z','deadline_utc':deadline.isoformat(),'finished_at_utc':now.isoformat(),'elapsed_budget_seconds':3600-(deadline-now).total_seconds(),'within_one_hour':now<=deadline,'attempts':attempts,'audio_controls':load(out/'strong_init/audio_controls/results.json'),'reward_shaping':'deferred at user request; not used','data_scope':'16 constructed training utterance groups; eight constructed development groups; no final test','source_hashes':{p.name:sha(p) for p in (ROOT/'scripts').glob('*grpo*.py')}}
write_json(out/'overall_summary.json',summary)
lines=['# GRPO continuation under a one-hour wall limit','','Binary execution rewards were retained. A stronger supervised initialization resolved the original all-zero reward cold start. This diagnostic is not a completed main experiment or proof that RL beats SFT.','',f"Finished at {now.isoformat()}; wall time from budget start {summary['elapsed_budget_seconds']/60:.1f} minutes. Within one hour: {summary['within_one_hour']}.",'','## Greedy checks','','| Attempt/checkpoint | Training (8 fixed groups) | Familiar-schema development (4 groups) | Development-only schema (4 groups) |','|---|---:|---:|---:|']
for name,item in attempts.items():
    result=item['result'] or {}
    for phase,key in [('Common parent','common'),('GRPO final','grpo_final'),('Continued SFT final','sft_control_final')]:
        data=result.get(key,{})
        def score(k):
            v=data.get(k);return f"{round(v['exact']*v['n'])}/{v['n']}" if v else 'unavailable'
        lines.append(f'| {name}: {phase} | {score("train")} | {score("dev_id")} | {score("dev_ood")} |')
lines+=['','## Fixed-seed sampled comparison','','Each row uses one fixed training schema/voice condition per utterance group, with four independent samples per prompt. All16 training and all8 development groups are included.','', '| Attempt/checkpoint | Training exact (64 samples) | Familiar-schema development exact (32 samples) |','|---|---:|---:|']
for name,item in attempts.items():
    for phase,data in (item['comparison'] or {}).items():
        def score(k):
            v=data.get(k);return f"{v['correct']}/{v['n']}" if v else 'unavailable'
        lines.append(f'| {name}: {phase} | {score("train")} | {score("dev_id")} |')
lines+=['','## Interpretation','','- Binary0/1 is the proposal’s full-program execution objective, not a GRPO requirement. All-zero and all-one groups have zero centered reward advantage.','- Shared SFT was essential. The first64-update continuation had useful gradients but no greedy accuracy gain; its small sampled training improvement has a bootstrap interval containing0.','- The stronger attempt inherited supervised weights only, added32 supervised updates, and branched a new common parent into64 GRPO and64 continued-SFT updates. Earlier RL weights were not inherited.','- The stronger GRPO trajectory corrected one familiar-schema dev temperature request from0 to16 degrees celsius, raising that fixed development probe score from1/4 to2/4. This is one case, and it recovers a score an earlier SFT checkpoint had already reached. It is not a broad generalization claim.','- Compare final GRPO with both its own common parent and its matched SFT control; a gain over the parent alone does not establish an advantage over SFT.','- No human-speech result or final-test result is available from this diagnostic. OOD schema success remains a separate concern.','- See per-attempt reports for utterance-cluster bootstrap intervals. They are descriptive on tiny dependent development samples.','','## Logs','','- [First attempt generations](generations.log)','- [Stronger attempt generations](strong_init/generations.log)','- [First attempt report and intervals](report.md)','- [Stronger attempt report and intervals](strong_init/report.md)','- [Reward rationale and references](reward_rationale.md)','- [Grounding controls](strong_init/audio_controls/results.json)','- [Complete machine-readable summary](overall_summary.json)','','Gold requests and calls appear in logs for auditing. They were not put into direct-audio rollout prompts. Raw IDs, detached old/reference scores, generation limits, rewards and resumed model states are retained.','','## Next step','','GRPO’s verifier, gradients and checkpoints are operational. Use a larger, preregistered pilot with sufficient shared SFT, real speech and a larger independent development set before committing to a main server comparison. Do not infer a paper-level advantage from this tiny development run.']
(out/'overall_report.md').write_text('\n'.join(lines)+'\n')
